  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-30\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n33169dcf75724f6190b5c14148553b52899936e0\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2012-06-08 11:04:11 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-790\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-790\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.stat.inference.MannWhitneyUTestTest::testBigDataSet\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.stat.inference.MannWhitneyUTest\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Mann-Whitney U Test Suffers From Integer Overflow With Large Data Sets\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nWhen performing a Mann-Whitney U Test on large data sets (the attached test uses two 1500 element sets), intermediate integer values used in calculateAsymptoticPValue can overflow, leading to invalid results, such as p-values of NaN, or incorrect calculations.\n\nAttached is a patch, including a test, and a fix, which modifies the affected code to use doubles\n\nComments:\n\n[James Pickering]: A patch, which adds a unit test for the issue, and a fix in the affected code\n\n[Mikkel Meyer Andersen]: Thank you very much for reporting this. I will have a look at this ASAP.\n\n[Mikkel Meyer Andersen]: This is fixed in SVN revision 1348024. Thanks again for reporting this issue.\n\n[Mikkel Meyer Andersen]: Thomas Neidhart suspect an overflow issues is still present.\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: As discussed on the ML, there may be still a problem with integer overflow in the code fragment below:\n\n{noformat}\nfinal double n1n2prod = n1 * n2;\n\n// http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mann%E2%80%93Whitney_U#Normal_approximation\nfinal double EU = n1n2prod / 2.0;\nfinal double VarU = n1n2prod * (n1 + n2 + 1) / 12.0;\n\nfinal double z = (Umin - EU) / FastMath.sqrt(VarU);\n{noformat}\n\nThe calculation of n1n2prod may still overflow if n1 and n2 are too big as it still does an int multiplication, so I would suggest to do it like that:\n\n{noformat}\nfinal long n1n2prod = (long) n1 * n2;\n\n// http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mann%E2%80%93Whitney_U#Normal_approximation\nfinal double EU = n1n2prod / 2.0;\nfinal double VarU = n1n2prod * (n1 + n2 + 1) / 12.0;\n\nfinal double z = (Umin - EU) / FastMath.sqrt(VarU);\n{noformat}",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.math3.stat.inference.MannWhitneyUTest (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.math3.stat.inference.MannWhitneyUTest (fixed)\n@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@\n                                              final int n2)\n         throws ConvergenceException, MaxCountExceededException {\n \n-        final int n1n2prod = n1 * n2;\n+        final double n1n2prod = n1 * n2;\n \n         // http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mann%E2%80%93Whitney_U#Normal_approximation\n         final double EU = n1n2prod / 2.0;"
}